From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] hvf: Activity Monitor counts guest RAM once (QEMU remaps its own view)

Applies after qemu-hvf-free-page-reclaim-reusable.patch.

What: a sweep remaps QEMU's own view of the VM's main RAM over itself
(mach_vm_remap, copy=FALSE, VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE), one
128 MB chunk at a time under the BQL, 20 ms apart; a pass a minute after
the start, then every 5 minutes, skipped while QEMU's footprint grew less
than 64 MB since the last pass, at most twice in a row (free page reports
can shrink the footprint while QEMU's touches grow it). The remap keeps the same VM objects at the
same offsets and drops only QEMU's page table entries; no page is touched,
copied or moved. Main RAM only, QEMU's private anonymous memory:
omacvm_ram_private(), which hvf_report_free_pages() now goes by too
(never the Venus host memory window's blobs, pflash, ROM, shared or
file-backed memory, nor while dirty logging is on).
A remap that would not do that turns the sweep off instead of stopping
QEMU: before the machine starts, a trial on 256 MB of scratch memory mapped
for the hypervisor as guest RAM is (hv_vm_map at an IPA no region of the
machine uses, else a second mapping), with a 4 MB piece given new memory as
a free page report leaves it, runs one chunk through the same steps, then
QEMU's view and a second mapping must read each other's writes; anything
else, or a trial past 3 s, and the sweep is off for the run ("off (why)").
Each chunk: its map entries must have the share mode the trial measured
(true shared on macOS 27), an object, be readable and writable and not
wired, else it stays as it is (counted, one qemu.log line); a spare mapping
of it (copy=FALSE) is made and checked; after the remap the entries are
read again at once (short region info): the same objects and offsets,
where a share mode read as private passes (the kernel reads a reference
count one low while a page is paged). Else the chunk is mapped back from
the spare (over what is mapped, into what is not) and the sweep stops for
the run, with how many us the view was wrong; QEMU stops (abort) only when
its view is still not the guest's memory after that. A failed remap that
left the view as it was, or no spare, stops the sweep for the run (one
line). -overcommit mem-lock turns it off. OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP=0 turns it
off; a number of seconds sets the time between passes (tests). qemu.log: a
start line ("own-view sweep: on" or "off (why)": omacvm check's "Activity
Monitor" row picks its words from it), a line an hour from the sweep's own
timer and one at exit (passes, passes skipped, chunks remapped and mapped
back, MB less in Activity Monitor, the main lock's hold per chunk: p99 and
longest, chunks left as they were, why it stopped);
OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP_CHECK=1 (tests) a line per pass. Test hook (test mode
only, OMACVM_TEST_SKIP_DISPLAYS): OMACVM_TEST_SWEEP_DIVERGE=canary|chunk
gives QEMU's view new memory after the trial's remap or after the first
remap of guest RAM's third chunk.

Why: macOS charges a page to a process's footprint once for every mapping
that touched it, resident or compressed. A guest page counts through the
hypervisor's map when the guest touches it, and again through QEMU's own
mapping once QEMU's threads did (disk reads into guest RAM, network,
graphics transfers): no memory, but Activity Monitor shows it. A 4 GB VM
on a Mac mini showed 2.1 GB more after its boot and 2.5 GB of reads; a
12 GB VM on a MacBook Pro M1 Max 1.2-2.0 GB more with nothing compressed
(work/tracks/vm-memory.md). A page only QEMU touched since the guest last
did leaves the count until one of them touches it again: the Mac still
holds it (ADR 0066). 3.2.17's sweep stopped QEMU when its first pass found
a remap had changed the view, and was tested on macOS 27 only; macOS 15 and
26 may do otherwise (ADR 0066, 3.2.18).

Upstream: OmacVM only (macOS accounting; upstream QEMU has no such sweep).
Test: Tests/memory/test-dcount.sh, no VM: guest RAM shared with a second
map or a real hv_vm_map; the trial passes and leaves nothing behind; QEMU
writes 1 GB, the guest reads it: the footprint is 2.0x what the Mac holds;
after one clean pass 1.001x (main, without the sweep: 2.0x, the test
fails); pass 1 runs while a thread preads and pwrites a file into and out
of guest RAM (buffered and F_NOCACHE) and with two free page reports
between chunks whose moves aside are released after the pass; every page
right as the guest sees it, and QEMU's writes seen by the guest and the
guest's by QEMU after it, the replaced ranges too; an idle pass skipped,
twice in a row at most; a chunk with a copy-on-write entry or one without
an object left as it is; a failed remap stops the sweep; --predicate:
which RAM blocks are swept; the test hook: the trial diverges or hangs (off,
no remap of guest RAM), a chunk diverges in the first or a later pass under
pread/pwrite, leaves a hole, reads private once, or its spare differs
(mapped back or stopped, memory the same both ways), mapping back fails
too (QEMU stops). The runtime build runs it on the patched source, CI on
this file.

diff --git a/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c b/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
index 8f450f29..ea65e27 100644
--- a/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
+++ b/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
@@ -722,11 +722,1119 @@ void hvf_report_free_pages_done(void)
 }
 /* omacvm-reclaim: end */
 
+/* omacvm-sweep: begin (app/runtime/Tests/memory/test-dcount.sh builds this part alone) */
+/*
+ * QEMU's own view of guest RAM, counted once (ADR 0066).
+ *
+ * macOS charges a page to a process's footprint (Activity Monitor's Memory)
+ * once for every mapping that touched it, resident or compressed: through
+ * the hypervisor's map when the guest touches it, and again through QEMU's
+ * own mapping once QEMU's threads did (disk reads into guest RAM, network,
+ * graphics transfers). Both mappings share the same VM objects (hv_vm_map
+ * makes them true shared), so the second count is no memory, but Activity
+ * Monitor shows it: a 4 GB VM showed 2.1 GB more after its boot and 2.5 GB
+ * of reads, and a compressed page keeps it until QEMU's mapping goes.
+ *
+ * The sweep remaps QEMU's view over itself (mach_vm_remap, copy=FALSE,
+ * VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE): the same objects at the same
+ * offsets, without QEMU's page table entries, so their charges go. No page
+ * is touched, copied or moved; QEMU's next touch maps a page again (about
+ * 0.4 us per 16 KiB page). A page only QEMU touched since the guest last
+ * did (a disk read the guest has not used yet) leaves the count until one
+ * of them touches it again; the Mac still holds it.
+ *
+ * Main RAM only, QEMU's private anonymous memory (omacvm_ram_private(), the
+ * rule a free page report goes by too), one 128 MB chunk (XNU's anonymous
+ * object) at a time under the BQL, 20 ms apart: a chunk never meets a free
+ * page report's replacement or its move aside, which run under the BQL too.
+ * A pass a minute after the start, then every 5 minutes, skipped while the
+ * footprint grew less than 64 MB since the last one, at most twice in a row
+ * (an idle VM; free page reports can shrink the footprint while QEMU's
+ * touches grow it, so at least every 15 minutes).
+ *
+ * Nothing on the Mac promises that such a remap keeps the same objects on
+ * every macOS, so the sweep checks it does, and turns itself off where it
+ * does not:
+ * - Before the machine starts, a trial on 256 MB of scratch memory mapped
+ *   for the hypervisor as guest RAM is (hv_vm_map at an IPA no region of the
+ *   machine uses, else a second mapping stands in), with a 4 MB piece given
+ *   new memory as a free page report leaves it and QEMU's view touching a
+ *   page every MB: its first chunk goes through the same steps as a chunk of
+ *   guest RAM, and then QEMU's view and a second mapping must read each
+ *   other's writes. Anything else, or a trial past 3 s (a kernel that wired
+ *   what the hypervisor maps would make the remap wait), and the sweep is
+ *   off for the run ("off (why)", the only start line) and never remaps
+ *   guest RAM. The trial also gives the share mode the hypervisor's mapping
+ *   makes (true shared on macOS 27): a chunk of guest RAM is remapped only
+ *   when every map entry has it, can be written and is not wired (else it
+ *   stays as it is and is counted, one qemu.log line).
+ * - Each chunk: its map entries read (short region info: no page looked
+ *   at); a spare mapping of them (mach_vm_remap, copy=FALSE: no page
+ *   touched) made and checked; the remap; at once the entries read again:
+ *   the same objects at the same offsets, writable. A share mode read as
+ *   private then still passes: the kernel reads an object's reference count
+ *   one low while one of its pages is paged in or out. The spare goes.
+ * - A remap that left QEMU's view other memory, or a hole, is mapped back
+ *   from the spare (over what is mapped there, into what is not: a delete
+ *   across a hole raises EXC_GUARD), and the sweep stops for the run with
+ *   the time QEMU's view was wrong: a disk, network or graphics transfer
+ *   through that chunk in that time may have gone wrong. QEMU stops (abort)
+ *   only when its view is still not the guest's memory after that. A failed
+ *   remap that left the view as it was, or no spare, stops the sweep for the
+ *   run (one line).
+ * Guest RAM wired by the kernel (mlock, -overcommit mem-lock, I/O to a raw
+ * disk device) would make the remap wait for it under the BQL: OmacVM.app
+ * has none of these, and mem-lock turns the sweep off.
+ *
+ * OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP=0 turns it off; a number of seconds sets the time
+ * between passes (tests). qemu.log: the start line, a line an hour and one
+ * at exit (passes, MB less in Activity Monitor, the main lock's hold per
+ * chunk); OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP_CHECK=1 (tests) a line per pass.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK (128ull << 20)
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_GAP_NS (20 * 1000000LL)
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_FIRST_S 60
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_PERIOD_S 300
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_GROWTH (64ull << 20)
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_SKIPS 2              /* passes skipped in a row at most */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS 8193            /* a chunk's 16 KiB pages, each its own object, and one */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL (256ull << 20) /* the trial's scratch memory; its first chunk is remapped */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_CUT (32ull << 20)   /* where a piece gets new memory, as a report leaves it */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_PIECE (4ull << 20)
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_MS 3000        /* the trial's time limit */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_RUNS 64
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's own private anonymous guest RAM: what a free page report may
+ * replace and the sweep may remap. Never shared, file-backed, device, ROM or
+ * flash memory, nor memory QEMU was given rather than allocated
+ * (RAM_PREALLOC: memory_region_init_ram_ptr, as the Venus host memory
+ * window's blobs), nor while dirty logging write-protects it.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_ram_private(MemoryRegion *mr)
+{
+    RAMBlock *rb = mr->ram_block;
+
+    return memory_region_is_ram(mr) && !mr->readonly && !mr->rom_device &&
+           !memory_region_is_ram_device(mr) && rb && rb->fd < 0 &&
+           !(rb->flags & (RAM_SHARED | RAM_PREALLOC)) &&
+           !memory_region_get_dirty_log_mask(mr);
+}
+
+/* A piece of QEMU's view: one object, from an offset on. */
+typedef struct OmacvmSweepRun {
+    mach_vm_address_t start, end;
+    uint64_t object, offset;
+} OmacvmSweepRun;
+
+/* Room for a chunk's pieces: as read before its remap, and as read again. */
+typedef struct OmacvmSweepBuf {
+    OmacvmSweepRun *runs, *again;
+    unsigned cap;
+} OmacvmSweepBuf;
+
+/* What a chunk's remap came to (omacvm_sweep_remap()). */
+typedef enum OmacvmSweepResult {
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_REMAPPED,              /* the same memory, without QEMU's page table entries */
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_LEFT,                  /* not as QEMU's view must be: left as it is */
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_UNCHANGED,             /* not remapped (no spare, the remap failed), the view as it was */
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_MAPPED_BACK,           /* the remap left the view other memory: mapped back */
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_LOST,                  /* the view is not the guest's memory, mapped back or not */
+} OmacvmSweepResult;
+
+typedef struct OmacvmSweepStats {
+    uint64_t passes, idle, chunks, less, left, left_bytes, mapped_back;
+    int64_t longest_ns;
+    uint32_t hold[OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS];  /* per chunk, in the reclaim's 0.1 ms steps */
+} OmacvmSweepStats;
+
+typedef struct OmacvmSweep {
+    uint8_t *host;                      /* main RAM in QEMU's view */
+    uint64_t size;
+    int64_t period_ns, next_ns;         /* between passes; until the next step */
+    uint64_t at;                        /* the next chunk; size: between passes */
+    bool stopped, said_left, check;
+    int mode;                           /* the share mode a chunk's entries must have (the trial's) */
+    bool trial_hv;                      /* the trial's memory was mapped by the hypervisor */
+    int64_t trial_ns;
+    unsigned skipped;                   /* passes skipped since the last one */
+    uint64_t footprint_after;           /* at the end of the last pass (0: none yet) */
+    int64_t hour_start;
+    char why[320];                      /* why it stopped */
+    OmacvmSweepStats hour, run;
+} OmacvmSweep;
+
+/* A chunk of guest RAM's pieces before a remap, and read again. */
+static OmacvmSweepRun omacvm_sweep_runs[OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS], omacvm_sweep_again[OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS];
+static OmacvmSweepBuf omacvm_sweep_buf = { omacvm_sweep_runs, omacvm_sweep_again, OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS };
+
+/* OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP: unset: on, every 5 minutes; "0": off; 10-86400: seconds between passes (tests). */
+static int64_t omacvm_sweep_period(const char *v)
+{
+    char *end;
+    long s;
+
+    if (!v || !*v) {
+        return OMACVM_SWEEP_PERIOD_S;
+    }
+    s = strtol(v, &end, 10);
+    if (*end || s < 0) {
+        return OMACVM_SWEEP_PERIOD_S;
+    }
+    if (s == 0) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return s < 10 ? 10 : s > 86400 ? 86400 : s;
+}
+
+static uint64_t omacvm_sweep_footprint(void)
+{
+    task_vm_info_data_t ti;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t n = TASK_VM_INFO_COUNT;
+
+    if (task_info(mach_task_self(), TASK_VM_INFO, (task_info_t)&ti, &n) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return ti.phys_footprint;
+}
+
+/* omacvm-sweep-test: begin */
+/*
+ * OmacVM tests only: a remap that does not do what ADR 0066 expects, at the
+ * chunk at `at` (OMACVM_TEST_SWEEP_DIVERGE in test mode, and
+ * Tests/memory/test-dcount.c). Every mach_vm_remap and mach_vm_region_recurse
+ * of the sweep goes through here; with `what` off they are only the calls.
+ *   CANARY, CHUNK  new memory over the page 1 MB into the chunk after its remap
+ *   SPARE          the same in the chunk's spare once it is made
+ *   HOLE           the remap leaves that page unmapped and fails
+ *   UNMAPPED       as HOLE, and every later remap into the chunk fails
+ *   DIP            the first read of the chunk after its remap says private
+ *   HANG           the remap waits hang_ms first
+ * skip: remaps of the chunk let through first (a later pass). The trial
+ * sets `at` for CANARY and HANG.
+ */
+enum {
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_OFF, OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_CANARY, OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_CHUNK,
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_SPARE, OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_HOLE, OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_UNMAPPED,
+    OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_DIP, OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_HANG,
+};
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_PAGE (1ull << 20)
+
+static struct {
+    int what;
+    mach_vm_address_t at;
+    unsigned skip;
+    int64_t hang_ms;
+    bool armed, done;
+} omacvm_sweep_test;
+
+static kern_return_t omacvm_sweep_test_remap(vm_map_t task, mach_vm_address_t *address,
+                                             mach_vm_size_t size, mach_vm_offset_t mask,
+                                             int flags, vm_map_t src_task,
+                                             mach_vm_address_t src, boolean_t copy,
+                                             vm_prot_t *cur, vm_prot_t *max,
+                                             vm_inherit_t inherit)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t at = omacvm_sweep_test.at, to = *address;
+    int what = omacvm_sweep_test.what;
+    bool over = at && (flags & VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE) && to == at;
+    bool into = at && !(flags & VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE) && to >= at && to < at + OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK;
+    bool spare = at && (flags & VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE) && src == at && !copy;
+    kern_return_t kr;
+
+    if (what == OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_UNMAPPED && omacvm_sweep_test.armed && into) {
+        return KERN_NO_SPACE;
+    }
+    if (what == OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_OFF || omacvm_sweep_test.done || !(over || spare)) {
+        return mach_vm_remap(task, address, size, mask, flags, src_task, src, copy, cur, max,
+                             inherit);
+    }
+    if (over && omacvm_sweep_test.skip) {
+        omacvm_sweep_test.skip--;
+        return mach_vm_remap(task, address, size, mask, flags, src_task, src, copy, cur, max,
+                             inherit);
+    }
+    if (what == OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_HANG && over) {
+        g_usleep(omacvm_sweep_test.hang_ms * 1000);
+    }
+    kr = mach_vm_remap(task, address, size, mask, flags, src_task, src, copy, cur, max, inherit);
+    if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        return kr;
+    }
+    switch (what) {
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_CANARY:
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_CHUNK:
+        if (over) {
+            mmap((void *)(uintptr_t)(at + OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_PAGE), vm_page_size,
+                 PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_FIXED | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON, -1, 0);
+            omacvm_sweep_test.done = true;
+        }
+        break;
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_SPARE:
+        if (spare) {
+            mmap((void *)(uintptr_t)(*address + OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_PAGE), vm_page_size,
+                 PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_FIXED | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON, -1, 0);
+            omacvm_sweep_test.done = true;
+        }
+        break;
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_HOLE:
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_UNMAPPED:
+        if (over) {
+            mach_vm_deallocate(mach_task_self(), at + OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_PAGE, vm_page_size);
+            omacvm_sweep_test.armed = omacvm_sweep_test.done = true;
+            return KERN_FAILURE;
+        }
+        break;
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_DIP:
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_HANG:
+        if (over) {
+            omacvm_sweep_test.armed = omacvm_sweep_test.done = true;
+        }
+        break;
+    }
+    return kr;
+}
+
+static kern_return_t omacvm_sweep_test_region(vm_map_t task, mach_vm_address_t *address,
+                                              mach_vm_size_t *size, natural_t *depth,
+                                              vm_region_recurse_info_t info,
+                                              mach_msg_type_number_t *count)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t want = *address;
+    kern_return_t kr = mach_vm_region_recurse(task, address, size, depth, info, count);
+
+    if (kr == KERN_SUCCESS && omacvm_sweep_test.what == OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_DIP &&
+        omacvm_sweep_test.armed && want == omacvm_sweep_test.at) {
+        omacvm_sweep_test.armed = false;
+        if (*count == VM_REGION_SUBMAP_SHORT_INFO_COUNT_64) {
+            ((vm_region_submap_short_info_64_t)info)->share_mode = SM_PRIVATE;
+        } else {
+            ((vm_region_submap_info_64_t)info)->share_mode = SM_PRIVATE;
+        }
+    }
+    return kr;
+}
+/* omacvm-sweep-test: end */
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's view of [at, at + len) as map entries: runs[] (*n of them, up to
+ * cap; one object's adjacent pieces as one) and *inherit. Before a remap
+ * (want: a share mode, the trial's) every entry has that share mode, an
+ * object, is readable and writable, not wired and inherited alike. After it,
+ * and in a spare (want -1), the objects and offsets the caller compares
+ * decide: any share mode but copy-on-write or empty passes (the kernel reads
+ * an object's reference count one low while one of its pages is paged, and
+ * true shared memory then reads private). Short region info: no page is
+ * looked at. "+N MB" in why counts from base.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_sweep_entries(mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_size_t len, int want,
+                                 OmacvmSweepRun *runs, unsigned cap, unsigned *n,
+                                 vm_inherit_t *inherit, mach_vm_address_t base,
+                                 char *why, size_t whylen)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t a = at, end = at + len, start;
+    vm_region_submap_short_info_data_64_t info;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t count;
+    mach_vm_size_t size;
+    natural_t depth;
+    uint64_t offset;
+    OmacvmSweepRun *r;
+    bool shared;
+
+    *n = 0;
+    while (a < end) {
+        start = a;
+        size = 0;
+        depth = 0;
+        count = VM_REGION_SUBMAP_SHORT_INFO_COUNT_64;
+        if (omacvm_sweep_test_region(mach_task_self(), &start, &size, &depth,
+                                     (vm_region_recurse_info_t)&info, &count) != KERN_SUCCESS ||
+            start > a) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "nothing mapped at +%llu MB",
+                     (unsigned long long)((a - base) >> 20));
+            return false;
+        }
+        shared = want >= 0 ? info.share_mode == want && !info.user_wired_count :
+                 info.share_mode != SM_COW && info.share_mode != SM_EMPTY;
+        if (info.is_submap || !shared || !info.object_id ||
+            (info.protection & (VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_WRITE)) != (VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_WRITE)) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "a map entry at +%llu MB is not shared with the "
+                     "guest as QEMU's view must be (share mode %d, %s, protection %d, "
+                     "%s)", (unsigned long long)((a - base) >> 20), info.share_mode,
+                     info.object_id ? "an object" : "no object", info.protection,
+                     info.user_wired_count ? "wired" : "not wired");
+            return false;
+        }
+        if (a == at) {
+            *inherit = info.inheritance;
+        } else if (want >= 0 && info.inheritance != *inherit) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "its map entries are inherited differently");
+            return false;
+        }
+        offset = info.offset + (a - start);
+        size = MIN(start + size, end) - a;
+        r = *n ? &runs[*n - 1] : NULL;
+        if (r && r->object == info.object_id && r->end == a &&
+            r->offset + (r->end - r->start) == offset) {
+            r->end = a + size;
+        } else if (*n == cap) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "more than %u map entries", cap);
+            return false;
+        } else {
+            runs[(*n)++] = (OmacvmSweepRun) { a, a + size, info.object_id, offset };
+        }
+        a += size;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Does [at, at + len) map exactly runs[] (n pieces, read at at0: each moved
+ * by at - at0), readable and writable? b->again holds what it maps.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_sweep_same(OmacvmSweepBuf *b, mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_address_t at0,
+                              mach_vm_size_t len, unsigned n, mach_vm_address_t base,
+                              char *why, size_t whylen)
+{
+    const OmacvmSweepRun *r, *c;
+    mach_vm_address_t d = at - at0;
+    vm_inherit_t inherit;
+    unsigned m, i;
+
+    if (!omacvm_sweep_entries(at, len, -1, b->again, b->cap, &m, &inherit, base, why, whylen)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (m != n) {
+        snprintf(why, whylen, "%u pieces before, %u after", n, m);
+        return false;
+    }
+    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        r = &b->runs[i];
+        c = &b->again[i];
+        if (r->start + d != c->start || r->end + d != c->end || r->object != c->object ||
+            r->offset != c->offset) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "another object or offset at +%llu MB",
+                     (unsigned long long)((c->start - base) >> 20));
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's view of [at, at + len) from the spare (copy=FALSE: the same objects
+ * at the same offsets), piece by piece: over what is mapped there
+ * (VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE), into what is not (VM_FLAGS_FIXED alone).
+ */
+static void omacvm_sweep_map_back(mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_size_t len,
+                                  mach_vm_address_t spare, vm_inherit_t inherit)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t a = at, end = at + len, start, stop, to;
+    vm_region_submap_short_info_data_64_t info;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t count;
+    mach_vm_size_t size;
+    vm_prot_t cur, max;
+    natural_t depth;
+    int flags;
+
+    while (a < end) {
+        start = a;
+        size = 0;
+        depth = 0;
+        count = VM_REGION_SUBMAP_SHORT_INFO_COUNT_64;
+        if (omacvm_sweep_test_region(mach_task_self(), &start, &size, &depth,
+                                     (vm_region_recurse_info_t)&info, &count) != KERN_SUCCESS ||
+            start >= end) {
+            start = end;                    /* nothing mapped from a on */
+        }
+        if (start > a) {
+            stop = start;
+            flags = VM_FLAGS_FIXED;
+        } else {
+            stop = MIN(start + size, end);
+            flags = VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE;
+        }
+        to = a;
+        omacvm_sweep_test_remap(mach_task_self(), &to, stop - a, 0, flags, mach_task_self(),
+                                spare + (a - at), FALSE, &cur, &max, inherit);
+        a = stop;
+    }
+}
+
+/* QEMU's view is not runs[]: map it back from the spare (0: none), twice at most. */
+static OmacvmSweepResult omacvm_sweep_restore(OmacvmSweepBuf *b, mach_vm_address_t base,
+                                              mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_size_t len,
+                                              unsigned n, vm_inherit_t inherit,
+                                              mach_vm_address_t spare, char *why, size_t whylen)
+{
+    char again[160] = "no spare to map back from";
+    size_t l;
+    int round;
+
+    for (round = 0; spare && round < 2; round++) {
+        omacvm_sweep_map_back(at, len, spare, inherit);
+        if (omacvm_sweep_same(b, at, at, len, n, base, again, sizeof(again))) {
+            return OMACVM_SWEEP_MAPPED_BACK;
+        }
+    }
+    l = strlen(why);
+    snprintf(why + l, whylen - l, "; then: %s", again);
+    return OMACVM_SWEEP_LOST;
+}
+
+/*
+ * One chunk of QEMU's view, [at, at + len), remapped over itself as ADR 0066
+ * says, under the BQL (the trial: on its own thread, before the machine
+ * starts): its entries checked (mode: the share mode they must have), a
+ * spare made and checked, the remap, at once its entries read again, then
+ * mapped back from the spare if they are not the same memory. *less: what
+ * QEMU's footprint dropped; *wrong_ns: how long the view was wrong. why
+ * says why when it is not OMACVM_SWEEP_REMAPPED.
+ */
+static OmacvmSweepResult omacvm_sweep_remap(OmacvmSweepBuf *b, int mode, mach_vm_address_t base,
+                                            mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_size_t len,
+                                            uint64_t *less, int64_t *wrong_ns,
+                                            char *why, size_t whylen)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t spare = 0, to = at;
+    vm_inherit_t inherit = VM_INHERIT_DEFAULT;
+    vm_prot_t cur = 0, max;
+    uint64_t before, after;
+    int64_t t0 = get_clock();
+    OmacvmSweepResult r;
+    bool spare_ok, same;
+    kern_return_t kr;
+    char what[160] = "", changed[160];
+    unsigned n;
+
+    *less = 0;
+    *wrong_ns = 0;
+    if (!omacvm_sweep_entries(at, len, mode, b->runs, b->cap, &n, &inherit, base, why, whylen)) {
+        return OMACVM_SWEEP_LEFT;
+    }
+    /* The spare: one more mapping of the same objects, to map back from. */
+    if (omacvm_sweep_test_remap(mach_task_self(), &spare, len, 0, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE,
+                                mach_task_self(), at, FALSE, &cur, &max,
+                                VM_INHERIT_NONE) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        spare = 0;
+        snprintf(what, sizeof(what), "making it failed");
+    }
+    spare_ok = spare && omacvm_sweep_same(b, spare, at, len, n, spare - (at - base), what,
+                                          sizeof(what));
+    if (!omacvm_sweep_same(b, at, at, len, n, base, changed, sizeof(changed))) {
+        snprintf(why, whylen, "making a spare changed QEMU's view at +%llu MB (%s)",
+                 (unsigned long long)((at - base) >> 20), changed);
+        r = omacvm_sweep_restore(b, base, at, len, n, inherit, spare_ok ? spare : 0, why, whylen);
+        *wrong_ns = get_clock() - t0;
+    } else if (!spare_ok) {
+        snprintf(why, whylen, "no spare mapping of the chunk at +%llu MB to map back from (%s)",
+                 (unsigned long long)((at - base) >> 20), what);
+        r = OMACVM_SWEEP_UNCHANGED;
+    } else {
+        before = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+        t0 = get_clock();
+        kr = omacvm_sweep_test_remap(mach_task_self(), &to, len, 0,
+                                     VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE, mach_task_self(), at,
+                                     FALSE, &cur, &max, inherit);
+        same = omacvm_sweep_same(b, at, at, len, n, base, what, sizeof(what));  /* at once */
+        if (same && kr == KERN_SUCCESS && to == at) {
+            after = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+            *less = before > after ? before - after : 0;
+            r = OMACVM_SWEEP_REMAPPED;
+        } else if (same) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "a remap at +%llu MB failed (%s)",
+                     (unsigned long long)((at - base) >> 20), mach_error_string(kr));
+            r = OMACVM_SWEEP_UNCHANGED;
+        } else {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "the remap at +%llu MB %schanged QEMU's view (%s)",
+                     (unsigned long long)((at - base) >> 20),
+                     kr != KERN_SUCCESS ? "failed and " : "", what);
+            r = omacvm_sweep_restore(b, base, at, len, n, inherit, spare, why, whylen);
+            *wrong_ns = get_clock() - t0;
+        }
+    }
+    if (spare) {
+        mach_vm_deallocate(mach_task_self(), spare, len);
+    }
+    return r;
+}
+
+/* Unmaps what is mapped in [at, at + len), around any hole. */
+static void omacvm_sweep_unmap_mapped(mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_size_t len)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t a = at, end = at + len, start;
+    vm_region_submap_short_info_data_64_t info;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t count;
+    mach_vm_size_t size;
+    natural_t depth;
+
+    while (a < end) {
+        start = a;
+        size = 0;
+        depth = 0;
+        count = VM_REGION_SUBMAP_SHORT_INFO_COUNT_64;
+        if (mach_vm_region_recurse(mach_task_self(), &start, &size, &depth,
+                                   (vm_region_recurse_info_t)&info, &count) != KERN_SUCCESS ||
+            start >= end) {
+            return;
+        }
+        size = MIN(start + size, end) - start;
+        mach_vm_deallocate(mach_task_self(), start, size);
+        a = start + size;
+    }
+}
+
+/* The trial (omacvm_sweep_canary()), on a thread of its own. */
+typedef struct OmacvmSweepTrial {
+    QemuMutex lock;
+    QemuCond cond;
+    bool done, abandoned;               /* under lock; abandoned: the trial's thread disposes of it */
+    hv_ipa_t ipa;                       /* where the hypervisor maps the scratch memory (0: nowhere) */
+    bool ok, hv;                        /* hv: it did (else a second mapping stood in) */
+    int mode;
+    int64_t ns;
+    char why[240];
+    OmacvmSweepRun runs[OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_RUNS], again[OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_RUNS];
+} OmacvmSweepTrial;
+
+static int omacvm_sweep_trials;        /* trial threads still running (a test waits for a late one) */
+
+static uint64_t omacvm_sweep_trial_mark(uint64_t o)
+{
+    return 0x6f6d616376000000ull + o;
+}
+
+/* QEMU's view writes a word every MB of the trial's chunk, every 256 KB in the new piece. */
+static uint64_t omacvm_sweep_trial_next(uint64_t o)
+{
+    return o >= OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_CUT && o < OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_CUT + OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_PIECE ?
+           o + (256 << 10) : o + (1 << 20);
+}
+
+/* After the trial's remap: do QEMU's view and a second mapping read what was there, and each other's writes? */
+static bool omacvm_sweep_trial_same(volatile uint64_t *view, volatile uint64_t *other,
+                                    char *why, size_t whylen)
+{
+    uint64_t o, i, mark;
+
+    for (o = 0; o < OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK; o = omacvm_sweep_trial_next(o)) {
+        i = o / sizeof(uint64_t);
+        mark = omacvm_sweep_trial_mark(o);
+        if (view[i] != mark || other[i] != mark) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "QEMU's view and a second mapping read other words at +%llu MB "
+                     "after a trial remap", (unsigned long long)(o >> 20));
+            return false;
+        }
+        view[i] = ~mark;
+        if (other[i] != ~mark) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "a second mapping does not see QEMU's view's write at +%llu MB "
+                     "after a trial remap", (unsigned long long)(o >> 20));
+            return false;
+        }
+        other[i] = mark ^ 0x5a;
+        if (view[i] != (mark ^ 0x5a)) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "QEMU's view does not see a second mapping's write at +%llu MB "
+                     "after a trial remap", (unsigned long long)(o >> 20));
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+static void *omacvm_sweep_trial_run(void *opaque)
+{
+    OmacvmSweepTrial *t = opaque;
+    OmacvmSweepBuf b = { t->runs, t->again, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_RUNS };
+    const hv_memory_flags_t flags = HV_MEMORY_READ | HV_MEMORY_WRITE | HV_MEMORY_EXEC;
+    const uint64_t cut = OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_CUT, piece = OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_PIECE;
+    mach_vm_address_t view = 0, standin = 0, other = 0, to;
+    bool whole = false, ends = false, lost = false, abandoned;
+    int64_t start = get_clock(), wrong;
+    char what[200] = "";
+    OmacvmSweepResult r;
+    vm_inherit_t inherit;
+    vm_prot_t cur, max;
+    uint8_t *scratch;
+    uint64_t align, less, o;
+    unsigned n;
+    int mode = -1, i;
+
+    scratch = qemu_anon_ram_alloc(OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL, &align, false, false);
+    if (!scratch) {
+        snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "no scratch memory for a trial remap");
+        goto out;
+    }
+    view = (mach_vm_address_t)(uintptr_t)scratch;
+    if (omacvm_sweep_test.what == OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_CANARY ||
+        omacvm_sweep_test.what == OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_HANG) {
+        omacvm_sweep_test.at = view;
+    }
+    /* The hypervisor maps it as it maps guest RAM; a second mapping stands in where it cannot. */
+    if (t->ipa && hv_vm_map(scratch, t->ipa, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL, flags) == HV_SUCCESS) {
+        whole = ends = t->hv = true;
+    } else if (mach_vm_remap(mach_task_self(), &standin, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL, 0, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE,
+                             mach_task_self(), view, FALSE, &cur, &max,
+                             VM_INHERIT_NONE) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        standin = 0;
+        snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "no second mapping of scratch memory for a trial remap");
+        goto out;
+    }
+    /* QEMU's view touches its pages (a disk read into guest RAM). */
+    for (o = 0; o < OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK; o += 1 << 20) {
+        *(volatile uint64_t *)(scratch + o) = omacvm_sweep_trial_mark(o);
+    }
+    /* A piece gets new memory, as a free page report leaves it: unmapped for the guest, new, mapped. */
+    if (whole) {
+        if (hv_vm_unmap(t->ipa + cut, piece) != HV_SUCCESS) {
+            snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "hv_vm_unmap of a piece of scratch memory failed");
+            goto out;
+        }
+        whole = false;
+    } else if (!ends && mmap((void *)(uintptr_t)(standin + cut), piece, PROT_NONE,
+                             MAP_FIXED | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON, -1, 0) == MAP_FAILED) {
+        snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "no room for a piece of scratch memory");
+        goto out;
+    }
+    if (mmap(scratch + cut, piece, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_FIXED | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON,
+             -1, 0) != (void *)(scratch + cut)) {
+        lost = true;
+        snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "no new memory for a piece of scratch memory");
+        goto out;
+    }
+    if (ends) {
+        if (hv_vm_map(scratch + cut, t->ipa + cut, piece, flags) != HV_SUCCESS) {
+            snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "hv_vm_map of a piece of scratch memory failed");
+            goto out;
+        }
+        whole = true;
+    } else {
+        to = standin + cut;
+        if (mach_vm_remap(mach_task_self(), &to, piece, 0, VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE,
+                          mach_task_self(), view + cut, FALSE, &cur, &max,
+                          VM_INHERIT_NONE) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+            snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "no second mapping of a piece of scratch memory");
+            goto out;
+        }
+    }
+    for (o = 0; o < OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK; o = omacvm_sweep_trial_next(o)) {
+        *(volatile uint64_t *)(scratch + o) = omacvm_sweep_trial_mark(o);
+    }
+    /* The share mode the hypervisor's mapping gives (three reads: a page being paged reads private). */
+    for (i = 0; i < 3 && mode < 0; i++) {
+        if (omacvm_sweep_entries(view, OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK, SM_TRUESHARED, b.runs, b.cap, &n,
+                                 &inherit, view, what, sizeof(what))) {
+            mode = SM_TRUESHARED;
+        } else if (omacvm_sweep_entries(view, OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK, SM_SHARED, b.runs, b.cap, &n,
+                                        &inherit, view, what, sizeof(what))) {
+            mode = SM_SHARED;
+        }
+    }
+    if (mode < 0) {
+        snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "scratch memory mapped as guest RAM is not shared as the "
+                 "sweep needs: %s", what);
+        goto out;
+    }
+    /* A second mapping of the chunk, to read QEMU's view's writes after the remap, and write to it. */
+    if (mach_vm_remap(mach_task_self(), &other, OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK, 0, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE,
+                      mach_task_self(), view, FALSE, &cur, &max, VM_INHERIT_NONE) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        other = 0;
+        snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "no second mapping for a trial remap's check");
+        goto out;
+    }
+    r = omacvm_sweep_remap(&b, mode, view, view, OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK, &less, &wrong, what,
+                           sizeof(what));
+    if (r != OMACVM_SWEEP_REMAPPED) {
+        lost = r == OMACVM_SWEEP_LOST;
+        snprintf(t->why, sizeof(t->why), "a trial remap on scratch memory: %s%s", what,
+                 r == OMACVM_SWEEP_MAPPED_BACK ? "; mapped back" : "");
+        goto out;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_sweep_trial_same((volatile uint64_t *)scratch,
+                                 (volatile uint64_t *)(uintptr_t)other, t->why, sizeof(t->why))) {
+        goto out;
+    }
+    t->mode = mode;
+    t->ok = true;
+out:
+    if (other) {
+        mach_vm_deallocate(mach_task_self(), other, OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK);
+    }
+    if (whole) {
+        hv_vm_unmap(t->ipa, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL);
+    } else if (ends) {
+        hv_vm_unmap(t->ipa, cut);
+        hv_vm_unmap(t->ipa + cut + piece, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL - cut - piece);
+    }
+    if (standin) {
+        mach_vm_deallocate(mach_task_self(), standin, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL);
+    }
+    if (lost) {
+        omacvm_sweep_unmap_mapped(view, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL);   /* a delete across a hole: EXC_GUARD */
+    } else if (scratch) {
+        qemu_anon_ram_free(scratch, OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL);
+    }
+    t->ns = get_clock() - start;
+    qemu_mutex_lock(&t->lock);
+    t->done = true;
+    abandoned = t->abandoned;
+    qemu_cond_signal(&t->cond);
+    qemu_mutex_unlock(&t->lock);
+    if (abandoned) {
+        qemu_cond_destroy(&t->cond);
+        qemu_mutex_destroy(&t->lock);
+        g_free(t);
+    }
+    __atomic_sub_fetch(&omacvm_sweep_trials, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Before the machine starts: the trial on scratch memory (the hypervisor
+ * maps it at ipa; 0: a second mapping stands in), at most limit_ms. true:
+ * the sweep may run (s->mode set); false: why says why not.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_sweep_canary(OmacvmSweep *s, hv_ipa_t ipa, int64_t limit_ms, char *why,
+                                size_t whylen)
+{
+    OmacvmSweepTrial *t = g_new0(OmacvmSweepTrial, 1);
+    int64_t deadline = get_clock() + limit_ms * 1000000LL, left;
+    QemuThread thread;
+    bool done, ok;
+
+    qemu_mutex_init(&t->lock);
+    qemu_cond_init(&t->cond);
+    t->ipa = ipa;
+    __atomic_add_fetch(&omacvm_sweep_trials, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
+    qemu_thread_create(&thread, "omacvm-sweep-trial", omacvm_sweep_trial_run, t,
+                       QEMU_THREAD_DETACHED);
+    qemu_mutex_lock(&t->lock);
+    while (!t->done && (left = deadline - get_clock()) > 0) {
+        qemu_cond_timedwait(&t->cond, &t->lock, (int)MAX(1, left / 1000000));
+    }
+    done = t->done;
+    t->abandoned = !done;
+    qemu_mutex_unlock(&t->lock);
+    if (!done) {
+        snprintf(why, whylen, "a trial remap on scratch memory took longer than %lld ms",
+                 (long long)limit_ms);
+        return false;
+    }
+    ok = t->ok;
+    if (ok) {
+        s->mode = t->mode;
+        s->trial_hv = t->hv;
+        s->trial_ns = t->ns;
+    } else {
+        snprintf(why, whylen, "%s", t->why);
+    }
+    qemu_cond_destroy(&t->cond);
+    qemu_mutex_destroy(&t->lock);
+    g_free(t);
+    return ok;
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_add_hold(OmacvmSweep *s, int64_t ns)
+{
+    int step = MIN(ns / OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS, OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1);
+
+    s->hour.hold[step]++;
+    s->run.hold[step]++;
+    s->hour.longest_ns = MAX(s->hour.longest_ns, ns);
+    s->run.longest_ns = MAX(s->run.longest_ns, ns);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_stop(OmacvmSweep *s, const char *why)
+{
+    s->stopped = true;
+    snprintf(s->why, sizeof(s->why), "%s", why);
+    warn_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: stopped for this run: %s; Activity Monitor "
+                "counts the VM's pages QEMU touches twice again, as up to 3.2.16", why);
+}
+
+/* One chunk of guest RAM, under the BQL (omacvm_sweep_remap()). */
+static void omacvm_sweep_chunk(OmacvmSweep *s)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t base = (mach_vm_address_t)(uintptr_t)s->host, at = base + s->at;
+    mach_vm_size_t len = MIN(OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK, s->size - s->at);
+    int64_t start = get_clock(), held, wrong;
+    char why[240], stop[320];
+    OmacvmSweepResult r;
+    uint64_t less;
+
+    s->at += len;
+    r = omacvm_sweep_remap(&omacvm_sweep_buf, s->mode, base, at, len, &less, &wrong, why,
+                           sizeof(why));
+    held = get_clock() - start;
+    switch (r) {
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_REMAPPED:
+        s->hour.chunks++;
+        s->run.chunks++;
+        s->hour.less += less;
+        s->run.less += less;
+        break;
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_LEFT:
+        s->hour.left++;
+        s->run.left++;
+        s->hour.left_bytes += len;
+        s->run.left_bytes += len;
+        if (!s->said_left) {
+            s->said_left = true;
+            warn_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: a chunk at +%llu MB stays as it is "
+                        "(%s); qemu.log's sweep lines count such chunks",
+                        (unsigned long long)((at - base) >> 20), why);
+        }
+        break;
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_UNCHANGED:
+        omacvm_sweep_stop(s, why);
+        break;
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_MAPPED_BACK:
+        s->hour.mapped_back++;
+        s->run.mapped_back++;
+        snprintf(stop, sizeof(stop), "mapped back after %lld us: %s; a disk, network or graphics "
+                 "transfer through that chunk in that time may have gone wrong",
+                 (long long)(wrong / 1000), why);
+        omacvm_sweep_stop(s, stop);
+        break;
+    case OMACVM_SWEEP_LOST:
+        error_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: QEMU's view of guest RAM at +%llu MB could not be "
+                     "mapped back (%s): QEMU stops before it reads or writes memory that is not "
+                     "the guest's", (unsigned long long)((at - base) >> 20), why);
+        abort();
+    }
+    omacvm_sweep_add_hold(s, held);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_log(const OmacvmSweep *s, const char *when,
+                             const OmacvmSweepStats *t)
+{
+    uint64_t total = 0, need, seen = 0;
+    char left[160] = "", back[64] = "", stopped[340] = "";
+    int64_t p99;
+    int step;
+
+    for (step = 0; step < OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS; step++) {
+        total += t->hold[step];
+    }
+    need = total - total / 100;
+    for (step = 0; step < OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1; step++) {
+        seen += t->hold[step];
+        if (seen >= need) {
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    p99 = MIN((int64_t)(step + 1) * OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS, t->longest_ns);
+    if (t->left) {
+        snprintf(left, sizeof(left), "; %" PRIu64 " chunks (%.0f MB) left as they were "
+                 "(not shared with the guest as QEMU's view must be)", t->left,
+                 t->left_bytes / 1048576.0);
+    }
+    if (t->mapped_back) {
+        snprintf(back, sizeof(back), ", %" PRIu64 " mapped back", t->mapped_back);
+    }
+    if (s->stopped) {
+        snprintf(stopped, sizeof(stopped), "; stopped: %s", s->why);
+    }
+    info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep %s: %" PRIu64 " passes over %.0f MB of guest "
+                "RAM, %" PRIu64 " skipped (QEMU's footprint grew less than 64 MB), %"
+                PRIu64 " chunks remapped%s; Activity Monitor %.0f MB less; main lock per "
+                "chunk p99 %.2f ms, longest %.2f ms%s%s", when, t->passes,
+                s->size / 1048576.0, t->idle, t->chunks, back, t->less / 1048576.0,
+                p99 / 1e6, t->longest_ns / 1e6, left, stopped);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_setup(OmacvmSweep *s, void *host, uint64_t size,
+                               int64_t period_s, bool check, int64_t now)
+{
+    memset(s, 0, sizeof(*s));
+    s->host = host;
+    s->size = size;
+    s->at = size;
+    s->mode = -1;                       /* none until the trial passed */
+    s->check = check;
+    s->period_ns = period_s * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND;
+    s->next_ns = MIN(period_s, OMACVM_SWEEP_FIRST_S) * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND;
+    s->hour_start = now;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Under the BQL, from the sweep's timer: the next chunk of a pass, or the
+ * start of one, and the hour's line. usable: main RAM is still QEMU's
+ * private memory (no dirty logging). Returns when to come again (ns from
+ * now), or -1: stopped for the run.
+ */
+static int64_t omacvm_sweep_step(OmacvmSweep *s, int64_t now, bool usable)
+{
+    uint64_t fp;
+
+    if (s->stopped) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+    if (now - s->hour_start >= 3600 * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND) {
+        omacvm_sweep_log(s, "in the last hour", &s->hour);
+        memset(&s->hour, 0, sizeof(s->hour));
+        s->hour_start = now;
+    }
+    if (!usable) {
+        s->at = s->size;                /* this pass ends here */
+        return s->period_ns;
+    }
+    if (s->at >= s->size) {
+        fp = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+        if (s->footprint_after && fp < s->footprint_after + OMACVM_SWEEP_GROWTH &&
+            s->skipped < OMACVM_SWEEP_SKIPS) {
+            s->skipped++;
+            s->hour.idle++;
+            s->run.idle++;
+            return s->period_ns;
+        }
+        s->skipped = 0;
+        s->at = 0;
+    }
+    omacvm_sweep_chunk(s);
+    if (s->stopped) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+    if (s->at < s->size) {
+        return OMACVM_SWEEP_GAP_NS;
+    }
+    s->hour.passes++;
+    s->run.passes++;
+    s->footprint_after = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+    if (s->check) {
+        info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep check: pass %" PRIu64 " done, %" PRIu64
+                    " chunks remapped this run, Activity Monitor %.0f MB less this run, "
+                    "longest chunk %.2f ms, footprint now %.0f MB", s->run.passes,
+                    s->run.chunks, s->run.less / 1048576.0, s->run.longest_ns / 1e6,
+                    s->footprint_after / 1048576.0);
+    }
+    return s->period_ns;
+}
+/* omacvm-sweep: end */
+
+/*
+ * The sweep's QEMU side: the trial when the machine is ready (before it
+ * starts), then the timer on the main loop (under the BQL).
+ */
+static OmacvmSweep omacvm_sweep;
+static QEMUTimer *omacvm_sweep_timer;
+static Notifier omacvm_sweep_init, omacvm_sweep_exit;
+static uint32_t omacvm_sweep_ipa_bits = 36;   /* the VM's IPA size (hvf_accel_init()) */
+
+/*
+ * Where the hypervisor maps the trial's scratch memory: size bytes on a
+ * 1 GB boundary just past one of the machine's regions, 4 GB up at least,
+ * below the VM's IPA size, that no region (or container) of the machine
+ * overlaps, so no vCPU or device reaches it and no later mapping lands
+ * there. 0: none.
+ */
+static hwaddr omacvm_sweep_free_ipa(uint64_t size)
+{
+    MemoryRegion *sys = get_system_memory(), *a, *b;
+    uint64_t top = 1ull << MIN(omacvm_sweep_ipa_bits, 63), c, e;
+
+    QTAILQ_FOREACH(a, &sys->subregions, subregions_link) {
+        e = a->addr + memory_region_size(a);
+        if (e < a->addr) {
+            continue;                   /* reaches the end of the address space */
+        }
+        c = ROUND_UP(e, 1ull << 30);
+        if (c < (4ull << 30) || c > top || top - c < size) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        QTAILQ_FOREACH(b, &sys->subregions, subregions_link) {
+            e = b->addr + memory_region_size(b);
+            if (b->addr < c + size && (e < b->addr || e > c)) {
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        if (!b) {
+            return c;
+        }
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_tick(void *opaque)
+{
+    MemoryRegion *mr = current_machine->ram;
+    int64_t next;
+
+    assert(bql_locked());
+    next = omacvm_sweep_step(&omacvm_sweep, get_clock(), omacvm_ram_private(mr));
+    if (next >= 0) {
+        timer_mod(omacvm_sweep_timer, qemu_clock_get_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME) + next);
+    }
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_at_exit(Notifier *n, void *data)
+{
+    omacvm_sweep_log(&omacvm_sweep, "this run", &omacvm_sweep.run);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_start(Notifier *n, void *data)
+{
+    MemoryRegion *mr = current_machine ? current_machine->ram : NULL;
+    const char *check = getenv("OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP_CHECK");
+    const char *test = getenv("OMACVM_TEST_SWEEP_DIVERGE");
+    const char *test_mode = getenv("OMACVM_TEST_SKIP_DISPLAYS");
+    int64_t period = omacvm_sweep_period(getenv("OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP"));
+    char why[240];
+
+    if (!period) {
+        info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: off (OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP=0): Activity "
+                    "Monitor counts the VM's pages QEMU touches twice");
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!mr || !mr->ram_block || !omacvm_ram_private(mr)) {
+        info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: off (the VM's RAM is not QEMU's private "
+                    "memory)");
+        return;
+    }
+    if (should_mlock(mlock_state)) {
+        info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: off (-overcommit mem-lock wires guest RAM): "
+                    "Activity Monitor counts the VM's pages QEMU touches twice");
+        return;
+    }
+    omacvm_sweep_setup(&omacvm_sweep, mr->ram_block->host, mr->ram_block->used_length,
+                       period, check && !strcmp(check, "1"), get_clock());
+    /*
+     * OmacVM tests only (test mode, the app drops the variable in a release
+     * build): new memory in QEMU's view after the trial's remap, or after the
+     * first remap of guest RAM's third chunk (256 MB in).
+     */
+    if (test && test_mode && *test_mode) {
+        if (!strcmp(test, "canary")) {
+            omacvm_sweep_test.what = OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_CANARY;
+        } else if (!strcmp(test, "chunk")) {
+            omacvm_sweep_test.what = OMACVM_SWEEP_TEST_CHUNK;
+            omacvm_sweep_test.at = (mach_vm_address_t)(uintptr_t)omacvm_sweep.host +
+                (omacvm_sweep.size > 3 * OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK ? 2 * OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK : 0);
+        }
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_sweep_canary(&omacvm_sweep, omacvm_sweep_free_ipa(OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL),
+                             OMACVM_SWEEP_TRIAL_MS, why, sizeof(why))) {
+        info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: off (%s): Activity Monitor counts the VM's pages "
+                    "QEMU touches twice", why);
+        return;
+    }
+    /* omacvm check's "Activity Monitor" row picks its words from this line. */
+    info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: on: QEMU remaps its view of the VM's %.0f MB "
+                "every %" PRId64 " s, so Activity Monitor counts the VM's pages once "
+                "(after a trial on scratch memory %s, %.1f ms; OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP=0 turns "
+                "it off)", omacvm_sweep.size / 1048576.0, period,
+                omacvm_sweep.trial_hv ? "mapped by the hypervisor" : "with a second mapping",
+                omacvm_sweep.trial_ns / 1e6);
+    omacvm_sweep_exit.notify = omacvm_sweep_at_exit;
+    qemu_add_exit_notifier(&omacvm_sweep_exit);
+    omacvm_sweep_timer = timer_new_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME, omacvm_sweep_tick, NULL);
+    timer_mod(omacvm_sweep_timer,
+              qemu_clock_get_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME) + omacvm_sweep.next_ns);
+}
